The dock apps here are other people's programs with one change, made in
November 2026: they draw themselves at Window Maker's GUI scale factor.
scale.h and the Makefile were written for wmutils and are under the GNU
General Public License, version 3 or later (../LICENSE), as is each program
as a whole in the form it has here.

wmclock/
  wmclock 1.0.16, from the dockapps collection of the Window Maker project
  (https://www.dockapps.net/wmclock, wmclock-1.0.16.tar.gz).
  Copyright (C) 1999 Jim Knoble <jmknoble@pobox.com>. Significant portions
  are derived from asclock by Beat Christen <spiff@longstreet.ch> and are
  copyright by Beat Christen and the other authors of asclock.
  GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
  Left out: the autoconf and automake files, README, INSTALL, ChangeLog
  and COPYING.
  Changed in wmclock.c: the window, its size hints and its shape mask are
  as many times larger as the scale factor, and the clock is copied to the
  window through scale_draw() of ../scale.h (drawWindow()); showTime()
  takes the size of the clock from the pixmap, not from the size hints.

wmacpi/
  wmacpi 2.4, from the same collection
  (https://www.dockapps.net/wmacpi, wmacpi-2.4.tar.gz).
  Copyright (C) 2000, 2001, 2002 timecop@japan.co.jp; rewritten by Simon
  Fowler <simon@himi.org>; see wmacpi/AUTHORS.
  GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
  Left out: the Makefile, README, INSTALL, ChangeLog, TODO and COPYING.
  Changed in wmacpi.c: the icon window, its size hints and its shape mask
  are as many times larger as the scale factor, and the pixmap is copied to
  the window through scale_draw() of ../scale.h, the pixmap no longer being
  the window's background when the factor is 2 or more.
